Aim: 
  Let Java programs — especially small ones / beginners’ code / script-like code — be written with far less boilerplate.

Motivation
    Some of the reasons behind this feature:
    Beginners often get confused / frustrated by the verbosity of even a simple “Hello, World” program: needing public class, public static void main(String[] args), etc. 
    The idea is to let small programs or scripts be written in a simpler way, without having to immediately learn about classes, packages, or static modifiers. 
    Also helps developers writing quick command-line tools or prototypes: less ceremony means faster iteration. 

